OctoDot includes material from these projects.

万象拼音 (rime-wanxiang)
  https://github.com/amzxyz/rime-wanxiang
  By amzxyz and contributors. Licensed under the Creative Commons
  Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0):
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  OctoDot's default lexicon, full-pinyin spellings and English word list
  are built from its dictionaries and spelling rules, at the release pinned
  in data/wanxiang.lock. OctoDot converts them to its own format: codes are
  normalized, rows it cannot read are left out, and the spelling rules are
  evaluated ahead of time. The English list is dicts/en.dict.yaml.

万象语法模型 (RIME-LMDG: wanxiang-lts-zh-hans.gram)
  https://github.com/amzxyz/RIME-LMDG
  By amzxyz. Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
  International License (CC BY 4.0):
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  OctoDot's sentence search reads this grammar model, unchanged, from the
  file pinned in data/grammar.lock, with the settings 万象's schema gives
  it.

FineWeb-2 (HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-2, cmn_Hani)
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-2
  By Hugging Face. Made available under the Open Data Commons Attribution
  License (ODC-By) v1.0: https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/by/1-0/
  OctoDot's reranker (rerank.weights, rerank.img) is a language model
  OctoDot trained on clauses of this dataset's Mandarin web text; its
  character set is the 8,000 most frequent characters there. The weights
  are released (data/rerank.lock) under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (LICENSE-weights).
  No text of the dataset is in the app.

librime-octagram
  https://github.com/lotem/librime-octagram
  © RIME Developers. Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License.
  engine/gram.h ports its file format (the header in gram_db.cc).
  engine/grammar.goose ports its key encoding and its Query
  (gram_encoding.cc, octagram.cc). engine/decoder.goose follows
  librime's sentence search (Poet's beam search, also BSD 3-Clause).

darts-clone
  https://github.com/s-yata/darts-clone
  © Susumu Yata. Licensed under the BSD 2-Clause License.
  engine/grammar.goose reads darts-clone's double-array units.

Unicode Character Database: Unihan
  https://www.unicode.org/reports/tr38/
  © Unicode, Inc. Licensed under the Unicode License v3:
  https://www.unicode.org/license.txt
  OctoDot marks each character of its lexicon with the character sets
  Unihan records for it (通用规范汉字表, GB2312, Big5), at the Unicode
  version pinned in data/unihan.lock.

Goose
  https://github.com/aardappel/goose
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:
  https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
  The OctoDot engine is written in Goose, and the Goose runtime's C is
  compiled into it.
